Closing the loop on NOV-2119 so Records has the decision in writing.<br />
<br />
The ticket: a partner noticed that the free-text "Scope Note" field we main=
tained on Casebridge matter records did not carry into Novarra. Confirmed, =
and it is not a defect - Novarra has no free-text scope field. Its "Matter =
Scope" is a controlled description populated at migration from the matter's=
 engagement-letter document class: for each migrated matter, the loader too=
k the description of the representation from the profiled engagement letter=
 and wrote it to the field. Where a scope changed after the engagement lett=
er, that change is reflected only if it exists as a profiled document (an a=
mendment or a supplemental letter). Free-text notes and anything recorded o=
nly in pre-2014 correspondence are not reflected.<br />
<br />
The vendor's position, which the steering committee accepted, is that the e=
ngagement letter is the authoritative scope document and the field works as=
 designed. The ticket is closed on that basis. Estimated population affecte=
d: closed matters opened before 2014 with a post-engagement scope note - a =
few hundred, none active.<br />
<br />
I flagged, and the minutes record, that for those matters Novarra's scope d=
escription can be less complete than what the file actually shows. Anyone r=
elying on the field for a pre-2014 matter should verify against the underly=
ing record - which for that era means the journal archive.<br />
